---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const SITE = 'https://dogtur.com';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy | Dogtur"
  description="Dogtur's editorial policy: research standards, vet-aware health rules, review independence, affiliate ethics, and corrections."
  canonical={`${SITE}/editorial-policy/`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <h2>Source context</h2>
    <p>
      Dogtur is an <strong>independent, experience-first senior-dog guide and
      review blog</strong> — not a veterinary authority. We write from
      research and real experience, and we defer to veterinarians on medical
      matters.
    </p>
    <h2>Health content rules (YMYL)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No diagnosis at a distance.</strong> We describe signs and say "discuss with your vet" — we never diagnose your dog.</li>
      <li><strong>No medication dosages.</strong> Medication content covers classes and vet conversations, never doses or schedules.</li>
      <li><strong>No cure or miracle claims.</strong> Supplements and therapies are covered with honest evidence framing.</li>
      <li><strong>Human painkiller warning.</strong> We explicitly warn against giving dogs human painkillers (e.g. ibuprofen, acetaminophen) unless a vet directs it.</li>
      <li><strong>Vet review where feasible.</strong> Health articles are fact-checked by a veterinarian where possible, with a named reviewer byline.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Review independence</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Rankings come from research and attributed evidence, never from commission rates.</li>
      <li>Every review discloses affiliate relationships at the top of the page.</li>
      <li>Negative findings are published. A product that fails our criteria gets a failing verdict.</li>
      <li>We have not yet completed hands-on testing. Until we do, no review claims test results of our own — other publications' testing is cited by name, and owner-review analysis is described as exactly that. When hands-on testing begins, this policy will require original evidence (photos, measurements) for every review.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Originality</h2>
    <p>
      Every article ships with original analysis: gap analysis against
      top-ranking sources, attributed synthesis of independent test findings,
      verified owner-review mining, or custom charts. We do not publish
      rewritten aggregations of other sites' content — and we never present
      attributed findings as our own testing. Original photos and hands-on
      test data will be added as that work is completed.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Factual errors are corrected promptly with a dated correction note at the
      top of the article. Report errors via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell sponsored placements inside editorial content. If that ever
      changes, sponsored content will be labeled and kept separate from tested reviews.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
